Bugfix: Avoid data race when canceling interactive password prompt

Canceling restic while it waited at an interactive password prompt could
race inside `ReadPassword`: the canceled call returned `context.Canceled`
while the still-running terminal read goroutine wrote the same named
error result. Password reading on cancel now keeps that worker's result
on a private channel, so the canceled path no longer shares mutable
return state.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22050
